%SIXMD 1
# @?CHMOD - CHANGE FILE MODE

## @?OPERANDS

### @?MODE
ONE TO FOUR OCTAL DIGITS.

### @?PATH
FILESYSTEM OBJECT WHOSE MODE IS TO BE CHANGED.

## DESCRIPTION

CHMOD SETS THE NATIVE FILE MODE OF ONE PATH FROM AN OCTAL MODE VALUE.
USAGE IS 'CHMOD MODE PATH'.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - SUCCESS
### @?1 - OPERATION FAILED OR CONDITION FALSE
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE WHEN APPLICABLE
